/* The slow eigenvalue solves lambda = j99 - rho^T (A - lambda I)^{-1} c.  At leading
 * order (lambda small vs spec(A)) the correction is rho^T A^{-1} c, which is 0 by the
 * entry above; so lambda_slow = j99 = -b.  Stated: if the Schur correction term S=0
 * and j99 = -b, then the leading-order slow eigenvalue equals -b. */
Problem
  \forall b \forall j99 \forall S \forall lambdaSlow
  ( S = 0 & j99 = -b & lambdaSlow = j99 - S  ->  lambdaSlow = -b )
End.
